Package: TRES
Type: Package
Title: Evidence-Gated Time-Varying Survival Modelling with Single-Cell-Defined Source Programs
Version: 0.1.0
Description: Implements TRES (Time-Resolved Effect Selection). Two null-calibrated evidence gates decide (1) which cell-source
    programs enter a clinically anchored Cox model and (2) whether covariate effects vary over follow-up time.
    When evidence is insufficient the model reverts to the static model. Time variation uses one
    shared smooth transition h(t; kappa, tau) with ridge shrinkage tuned by leave-one-cohort-out integrated
    Brier score. Includes single-sample, platform-agnostic program scoring.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2)
Imports: survival, stats
